<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Open-Source on Petro Ladkin</title><link>https://petroladkin.dev/categories/open-source/</link><description>Recent content in Open-Source on Petro Ladkin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://petroladkin.dev/categories/open-source/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>hookwitness</title><link>https://petroladkin.dev/portfolio/hookwitness/</link><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://petroladkin.dev/portfolio/hookwitness/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Catch webhooks, get a verdict, attach the evidence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Status:&lt;/strong&gt; 0.2 (&lt;a href="https://github.com/petroladkin/hookwitness/releases/tag/v0.2.0"&gt;v0.2.0&lt;/a&gt;, October 2026). The catcher, scripted replies, verdicts, reports, the REST API and the MCP server work, with users and login, replay and setup files. Until 1.0 a minor version may change the API or the flags. Apache License 2.0.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/petroladkin/hookwitness/v0.2.0/docs/images/demo.gif" alt="A 20-second run: GitHub webhooks arrive live on the register; the third is answered 503 by a rule; one signed with the wrong secret turns red and its page says the signature does not match; then the report is downloaded and opened"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>